{"id":"mahabharata-7-091","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":91,"title":"एकनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 91 · Satyaki and Kritavarman","summary":{"en":"Satyaki fights the Kaurava elephant division and Jalasandha, while Kritavarman holds back the Pandavas. The battle between Satyaki and the Kuru warriors and Drona grows fierce.","kn":"ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಕೌರವ ಆನೆದಳ ಮತ್ತು ಜಲಸಂಧನೊಡನೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃತವರ್ಮ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ತಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಮತ್ತು ಕುರುವೀರರು, ದ್ರೋಣನ ನಡುವಿನ ಯುದ್ಧ ಉಗ್ರವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"सात्यकि कौरव गज-सेना और जलसन्ध से लड़ता है, जबकि कृतवर्मा पाण्डवों को रोकता है। सात्यकि और कुरु योद्धाओं तथा द्रोण का युद्ध उग्र हो जाता है।","te":"సాత్యకి కౌరవ గజసేనతో, జలసంధునితో పోరాడతాడు, కృతవర్మ పాండవులను ఆపుతాడు. సాత్యకి, కురు యోధులు, ద్రోణుల మధ్య యుద్ధం తీవ్రమవుతుంది.","ta":"சாத்யகி கௌரவ யானைப்படையோடும் ஜலசந்தனோடும் போரிட, கிருதவர்மன் பாண்டவரைத் தடுக்கிறான். சாத்யகிக்கும் குரு வீரருக்கும் த்ரோணருக்குமிடையே போர் கடுமையாகிறது.","ml":"സാത്യകി കൗരവ ആനപ്പടയോടും ജലസന്ധനോടും പൊരുതുന്നു; കൃതവർമാവ് പാണ്ഡവരെ പിടിച്ചുനിർത്തുന്നു. സാത്യകിയും കൗരവ യോദ്ധാക്കളും തമ്മിലും ദ്രോണരുമായുമുള്ള പോര് കടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.91; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शृणुष्वैकमना राजन्यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ।\nद्राव्यमाणे बले तस्मिन्हार्दिक्येन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen with a single mind, O king, to what you ask me, how that army was driven back by the great-souled Hridika's son."}},{"n":2,"text":"लज्जयावनते चापि प्रहृष्टैश्चैव तावकैः ।\nद्वीपो य आसीत्पाण्डूनामगाधे गाधमिच्छताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Pandavas bowed their heads in shame and your men were elated, the one who was an island for the Pandavas, like a foothold for those seeking one in deep water,"}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु निनदं भीमं तावकानां महाहवे ।\nशैनेयस्त्वरितो राजन्कृतवर्माणमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heard the dreadful roar of your men in the great battle, and Shaineya quickly went toward Kritavarman, O king."}},{"n":4,"text":"कृतवर्मा तु हार्दिक्यः शैनेयं निशितैः शरैः ।\nअवाकिरत्सुसंक्रुद्धस्ततोऽक्रुध्यत सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hridika's son Kritavarman, in great anger, showered Shaineya with sharp arrows, and Satyaki grew angry."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः सुनिशितं भल्लं शैनेयः कृतवर्मणे ।\nप्रेषयामास समरे शरांश्च चतुरोऽपरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shaineya sent a very sharp broad-headed arrow at Kritavarman in the battle, and four other arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते तस्य जघ्निरे वाहान्भल्लेनास्याच्छिनद्धनुः ।\nपृष्ठरक्षं तथा सूतमविध्यन्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those killed his horses; with the broad-headed arrow he cut his bow, and he struck his rear guard and charioteer with sharp arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततस्तं विरथं कृत्वा सात्यकिः सत्यविक्रमः ।\nसेनामस्यार्दयामास शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having left him without a chariot, Satyaki, whose valor is true, tormented his troops with straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":8,"text":"साभज्यताथ पृतना शैनेयशरपीडिता ।\nततः प्रायाद्वै त्वरितः सात्यकिः सत्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormented by Shaineya's arrows, that army broke, and Satyaki, whose valor is true, went quickly on."}},{"n":9,"text":"शृणु राजन्यदकरोत्तव सैन्येषु वीर्यवान् ।\nअतीत्य स महाराज द्रोणानीकमहार्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, O king, what that mighty one did among your troops. Having crossed the great ocean of Drona's host,"}},{"n":10,"text":"पराजित्य च संहृष्टः कृतवर्माणमाहवे ।\nयन्तारमब्रवीच्छूरः शनैर्याहीत्यसंभ्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And having defeated Kritavarman in the fight and rejoicing, the hero told his charioteer, \"Go slowly and without hurry.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु तव तत्सैन्यं रथाश्वद्विपसंकुलम् ।\nपदातिजनसंपूर्णमब्रवीत्सारथिं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your army crowded with chariots, horses and elephants and full of foot soldiers, he again spoke to his charioteer."}},{"n":12,"text":"यदेतन्मेघसंकाशं द्रोणानीकस्य सव्यतः ।\nसुमहत्कुञ्जरानीकं यस्य रुक्मरथो मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That huge elephant force like clouds on the left of Drona's army, led by Rukmaratha,"}},{"n":13,"text":"एते हि बहवः सूत दुर्निवार्याश्च संयुगे ।\nदुर्योधनसमादिष्टा मदर्थे त्यक्तजीविताः ।\nराजपुत्रा महेष्वासाः सर्वे विक्रान्तयोधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many of them, charioteer, hard to check in battle, were ordered by Duryodhana to stand for me, ready to give up their lives, all princes, mighty bowmen, valiant fighters."}},{"n":14,"text":"त्रिगर्तानां रथोदाराः सुवर्णविकृतध्वजाः ।\nमामेवाभिमुखा वीरा योत्स्यमाना व्यवस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The noble chariot-fighters of the Trigartas, with golden-wrought banners, stand facing me alone, ready to fight."}},{"n":15,"text":"अत्र मां प्रापय क्षिप्रमश्वांश्चोदय सारथे ।\nत्रिगर्तैः सह योत्स्यामि भारद्वाजस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take me quickly there, charioteer, and urge the horses on. I shall fight the Trigartas in sight of Bharadvaja's son.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः प्रायाच्छनैः सूतः सात्वतस्य मते स्थितः ।\nरथेनादित्यवर्णेन भास्वरेण पताकिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the charioteer, following the Satvata's wish, went slowly on in a chariot bright as the sun, shining, with pennants."}},{"n":17,"text":"तमूहुः सारथेर्वश्या वल्गमाना हयोत्तमाः ।\nवायुवेगसमाः संख्ये कुन्देन्दुरजतप्रभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His best horses, obedient to the charioteer, prancing, swift as the wind in battle, bright as jasmine, moon and silver, bore him."}},{"n":18,"text":"आपतन्तं रथं तं तु शङ्खवर्णैर्हयोत्तमैः ।\nपरिवव्रुस्ततः शूरा गजानीकेन सर्वतः ।\nकिरन्तो विविधांस्तीक्ष्णान्सायकाँल्लघुवेधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that chariot with its conch-white excellent horses came on, the heroes surrounded it on every side with a force of elephants, showering various sharp arrows that pierce lightly."}},{"n":19,"text":"सात्वतोऽपि शितैर्बाणैर्गजानीकमयोधयत् ।\nपर्वतानिव वर्षेण तपान्ते जलदो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Satvata too fought the elephant force with keen arrows, as a great cloud at the close of summer rains on mountains."}},{"n":20,"text":"वज्राशनिसमस्पर्शैर्वध्यमानाः शरैर्गजाः ।\nप्राद्रवन्रणमुत्सृज्य शिनिवीर्यसमीरितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by arrows with touch like thunderbolts, driven by Shini's grandson's strength, the elephants left the battlefield and fled."}},{"n":21,"text":"शीर्णदन्ता विरुधिरा भिन्नमस्तकपिण्डकाः ।\nविशीर्णकर्णास्यकरा विनियन्तृपताकिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their tusks shattered, bloodless, their forehead lumps split, with ears, mouths and trunks torn, their drivers and flags lost,"}},{"n":22,"text":"संभिन्नवर्मघण्टाश्च संनिकृत्तमहाध्वजाः ।\nहतारोहा दिशो राजन्भेजिरे भ्रष्टकम्बलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With armor and bells broken, great banners cut down, their riders killed and blankets fallen, they fled in all directions, O king,"}},{"n":23,"text":"रुवन्तो विविधान्रावाञ्जलदोपमनिस्वनाः ।\nनाराचैर्वत्सदन्तैश्च सात्वतेन विदारिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crying various cries, with voices like thunderclouds, torn apart by the Satvata's iron arrows and vatsadantas."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्मिन्द्रुते गजानीके जलसंधो महारथः ।\nयत्तः संप्रापयन्नागं रजताश्वरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that elephant force fled, the great chariot-warrior Jalasandha, steadily, drove his elephant toward the silver-horsed chariot."}},{"n":25,"text":"रुक्मवर्णकरः शूरस्तपनीयाङ्गदः शुचिः ।\nकुण्डली मुकुटी शङ्खी रक्तचन्दनरूषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brave, with golden-colored arms, with gold armlets, clean, wearing earrings, crown and conch, smeared with red sandal,"}},{"n":26,"text":"शिरसा धारयन्दीप्तां तपनीयमयीं स्रजम् ।\nउरसा धारयन्निष्कं कण्ठसूत्रं च भास्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wearing on his head a shining garland of gold, and on his chest a nishka and a bright necklace,"}},{"n":27,"text":"चापं च रुक्मविकृतं विधुन्वन्गजमूर्धनि ।\nअशोभत महाराज सविद्युदिव तोयदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaking his bow wrought with gold on the elephant's head, he looked splendid, great king, like a cloud with lightning."}},{"n":28,"text":"तमापतन्तं सहसा मागधस्य गजोत्तमम् ।\nसात्यकिर्वारयामास वेलेवोद्वृत्तमर्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki checked the finest elephant of the Magadha king as it suddenly rushed on, as the shore checks a surging sea."}},{"n":29,"text":"नागं निवारितं दृष्ट्वा शैनेयस्य शरोत्तमैः ।\nअक्रुध्यत रणे राजञ्जलसंधो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his elephant checked by Shaineya's best arrows, the mighty Jalasandha, O king, grew angry in battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महेष्वासो मार्गणैर्भारसाधनैः ।\nअविध्यत शिनेः पौत्रं जलसंधो महोरसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty bowman Jalasandha, enraged, struck the grandson of Shini in the broad chest with heavy-bearing arrows."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततोऽपरेण भल्लेन पीतेन निशितेन च ।\nअस्यतो वृष्णिवीरस्य निचकर्त शरासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with another yellow, sharp broad-headed arrow he cut the bow of the Vrishni hero as he was shooting."}},{"n":32,"text":"सात्यकिं छिन्नधन्वानं प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nअविध्यन्मागधो वीरः पञ्चभिर्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Satyaki with his bow cut, the Magadha hero, as though laughing, pierced him with five sharp arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":33,"text":"स विद्धो बहुभिर्बाणैर्जलसंधेन वीर्यवान् ।\nनाकम्पत महाबाहुस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by many arrows from Jalasandha, the mighty-armed and powerful Satyaki did not tremble, which was a wonder."}},{"n":34,"text":"अचिन्तयन्वै स शरान्नात्यर्थं संभ्रमाद्बली ।\nधनुरन्यत्समादाय तिष्ठ तिष्ठेत्युवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strong one thought nothing of those arrows and, without much flurry, took another bow and said, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":35,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा शैनेयो जलसंधं महोरसि ।\nविव्याध षष्ट्या सुभृशं शराणां प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said only this, Shaineya, as though laughing, struck Jalasandha hard in the chest with sixty arrows."}},{"n":36,"text":"क्षुरप्रेण च पीतेन मुष्टिदेशे महद्धनुः ।\nजलसंधस्य चिच्छेद विव्याध च त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a yellow razor-headed arrow he cut Jalasandha's great bow at the grip, and struck him with three arrows."}},{"n":37,"text":"जलसंधस्तु तत्त्यक्त्वा सशरं वै शरासनम् ।\nतोमरं व्यसृजत्तूर्णं सात्यकिं प्रति मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jalasandha threw aside that bow with its arrow and quickly hurled a javelin at Satyaki, O lord."}},{"n":38,"text":"स निर्भिद्य भुजं सव्यं माधवस्य महारणे ।\nअभ्यगाद्धरणीं घोरः श्वसन्निव महोरगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It pierced the left arm of the Madhava in the great battle and went to the earth, dreadful, like a hissing great serpent."}},{"n":39,"text":"निर्भिन्ने तु भुजे सव्ये सात्यकिः सत्यविक्रमः ।\nत्रिंशद्भिर्विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैर्जलसंधमताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his left arm pierced, Satyaki, whose valor is true, struck Jalasandha with thirty sharp arrows."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रगृह्य तु ततः खड्गं जलसंधो महाबलः ।\nआर्षभं चर्म च महच्छतचन्द्रमलंकृतम् ।\nतत आविध्य तं खड्गं सात्वतायोत्ससर्ज ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty Jalasandha took a sword and a great bull-hide shield adorned with a hundred moons, whirled the sword and flung it at the Satvata."}},{"n":41,"text":"शैनेयस्य धनुश्छित्त्वा स खड्गो न्यपतन्महीम् ।\nअलातचक्रवच्चैव व्यरोचत महीं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It cut Shaineya's bow and fell to the ground, and, lying on the earth, shone like a whirling firebrand."}},{"n":42,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय सर्वकायावदारणम् ।\nशालस्कन्धप्रतीकाशमिन्द्राशनिसमस्वनम् ।\nविस्फार्य विव्यधे क्रुद्धो जलसंधं शरेण ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, taking another bow, one that tears through every body, like the trunk of a sala tree, sounding like Indra's thunderbolt, he drew it and, enraged, struck Jalasandha with an arrow."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततः साभरणौ बाहू क्षुराभ्यां माधवोत्तमः ।\nसाङ्गदौ जलसंधस्य चिच्छेद प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the best of the Madhavas, as though laughing, cut off Jalasandha's two arms, with their ornaments and armlets, with two razor-headed arrows."}},{"n":44,"text":"तौ बाहू परिघप्रख्यौ पेततुर्गजसत्तमात् ।\nवसुंधराधराद्भ्रष्टौ पञ्चशीर्षाविवोरगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two arms, like iron bars, fell from the finest of elephants, like two five-headed serpents fallen from a mountain."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः सुदंष्ट्रं सुहनु चारुकुण्डलमुन्नसम् ।\nक्षुरेणास्य तृतीयेन शिरश्चिच्छेद सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki, with a third razor-headed arrow, cut off his head, with its fine teeth, lovely jaw, beautiful earrings and handsome nose."}},{"n":46,"text":"तत्पातितशिरोबाहुकबन्धं भीमदर्शनम् ।\nद्विरदं जलसंधस्य रुधिरेणाभ्यषिञ्चत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The terrible-looking trunk, with its head and arms fallen, drenched Jalasandha's elephant with blood."}},{"n":47,"text":"जलसंधं निहत्याजौ त्वरमाणस्तु सात्वतः ।\nनैषादिं पातयामास गजस्कन्धाद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed Jalasandha in the fight, the Satvata, in haste, cast down the elephant's driver, the Nishada, from the elephant's neck, O lord of the people."}},{"n":48,"text":"रुधिरेणावसिक्ताङ्गो जलसंधस्य कुञ्जरः ।\nविलम्बमानमवहत्संश्लिष्टं परमासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jalasandha's elephant, its body drenched in blood, bore on, the corpse hanging and clinging to its fine seat."}},{"n":49,"text":"शरार्दितः सात्वतेन मर्दमानः स्ववाहिनीम् ।\nघोरमार्तस्वरं कृत्वा विदुद्राव महागजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormented by the Satvata's arrows, trampling its own army, the great elephant gave a terrible cry of pain and ran away."}},{"n":50,"text":"हाहाकारो महानासीत्तव सैन्यस्य मारिष ।\nजलसंधं हतं दृष्ट्वा वृष्णीनामृषभेण ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great wail went up from your army, my lord, when it saw Jalasandha slain by the bull of the Vrishnis."}},{"n":51,"text":"विमुखाश्चाभ्यधावन्त तव योधाः समन्ततः ।\nपलायने कृतोत्साहा निरुत्साहा द्विषज्जये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your warriors ran in all directions with faces turned away, eager only to flee and no longer keen to beat the enemy."}},{"n":52,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे राजन्द्रोणः शस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nअभ्ययाज्जवनैरश्वैर्युयुधानं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meanwhile, O king, Drona, best of weapon-bearers, came on with swift horses against the great chariot-warrior Yuyudhana."}},{"n":53,"text":"तमुदीर्णं तथा दृष्ट्वा शैनेयं कुरुपुंगवाः ।\nद्रोणेनैव सह क्रुद्धाः सात्यकिं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Shaineya so swollen with success, the Kuru leaders, enraged, surrounded Satyaki together with Drona."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं कुरूणां सात्वतस्य च ।\nद्रोणस्य च रणे राजन्घोरं देवासुरोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a battle began between the Kurus and the Satvata, and Drona, in the fight, O king, dreadful and like that of the gods and asuras."}}]}]}